      ],
      "source": "https://newmexicotravelguy.com/church-rock/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "On July 16, 1979, a uranium mill spill released 1,100 tons of ore into the Puerco River, the largest radioactive release in the U.S.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church_Rock%2C_New_Mexico"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2003, the Churchrock Chapter launched the Uranium Monitoring Project to study abandoned mine impacts and build community research capacity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church_Rock%2C_New_Mexico"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Locally known as Tsé Íí’áhí, the formation means 'rock church' in Navajo.",
